        "id": 1960706
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T05:03:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMHO, there will be anyways a runtime check required for None.\nWhen it receives NonZeroU16::new(0) the value will be None. So anyways this needs to be checked at runtime. Or an unwrap() when it is None would lead to a panic.\nInstead, I can use panic directly like below\n\nlet mq \u003d match num_queues {\n    0 \u003d\u003e panic(\"Number of queues cannot be zero for a block device\");\n    1 \u003d\u003e false,\n    _ \u003d\u003e true,\n    };",
      "parentUuid": "f11222bf_9bfea4d7",
      "revId": "583c2964a15e0c419babe8862e9c5045ba666545",
